<title>AUSTRIA: Libyan oil minister downplays Iraq deal acceptance.</title>
<headline>Libyan oil minister downplays Iraq deal acceptance.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Libyan oil minister Abdullah Salem al-Badri downplayed the impact of Iraq's acceptance of the terms of a limited oil for food deal on OPEC's meeting due to start here on Wednesday</p>
<p>&quot;Nothing will happen, we will find a way out,&quot; Badri said when questioned by lobby reporters on the impact of Iraq's statement.  </p>
<p>Iraqi ambassador to the U.N. Nizar Hamdoon said on Monday in New York that Baghdad had accepted U.N. conditions for the limited oil exports deal and said oil could start flowing in December.</p>
<p>When asked whether OPEC's meeting may end on Thursday, Badri replied &quot;I hope so.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Vienna Newsroom +431 713 2034</p>
